# Maiolino et al. (2024), A&A 691, A145 (arXiv:2308.01230v4, post-acceptance), Table 4: density of broad-line (type-1) AGN hosts in JADES
# Redshift: 4 < z < 6 (Bouwens et al. 2021 z~5 galaxy LF used as the reference)
# Magnitude definition: total (AGN+host) absolute UV magnitude M_UV (not M1450) -> M1500
# Phi convention: log10(Phi / cMpc^-3 mag^-1), asymmetric errors in dex (upper, lower); bins of +-0.75 mag
# Note: Phi = f_AGN(M_UV) x Bouwens+21 galaxy UV LF, for AGN with L_bol > 1e44 erg/s; errors combine Poisson, cosmic
#       variance and the inclusion/exclusion of three AGN targeted for their NIRCam appearance.
# Note: the paper also lists conservative lower limits log Phi_min > -5.73 (M_UV = -18.0) and > -5.98 (-19.5); not included.
# Note: the two rows were previously swapped between the magnitude bins (fixed; same values in arXiv v1 and v4).
#
# M_UV  LogPhi  UpperDelta  LowerDelta
-18.0  -3.06  0.18  0.26
-19.5  -3.83  0.23  0.44
